| Area | Impact |
|------|--------|
| **Security / Stability** | Immediate access to latest patches; avoids risk of running an unsupported runtime. |
| **Upgrade effort** | Small one‑step bump to 3.5.16, then a planned migration to 4.x; mitigates “big‑bang” upgrade pain. |
| **Developer experience** | Spring Boot 4 introduces Java 25 language features (records, sealed interfaces, pattern matching) and improved auto‑configuration, reducing boilerplate. |
| **Observability** | Native Datadog integration cuts down on custom instrumentation code. |
| **Cloud‑native readiness** | Enhanced Kubernetes support (readiness probes, layered Docker images) speeds container build & rollout cycles. |
| **CI/CD** | Updating GitHub Actions to JDK 25 aligns the build pipeline with production runtime, preventing “works‑locally” issues. |

